1
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes fly off too,

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,960
onto the head of the
carpenter who was chopping away,

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Katsushika, Kameari,
another yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed-hat water pitcher,

9
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:07,460
the sunset falls into the great sky.

10
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:15,920
Why does tomorrow end too

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,080
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness lost again.

12
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:25,860
Aaaaaah!

13
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:30,760
Four... what?

14
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:36,420
Gah!

15
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:38,660
No!

16
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:49,180
Do you want this child to get hurt?
Stop this stupid stunt!

17
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:51,200
Ryotsu! Release the hostage at once!

18
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:54,480
Shut up! Take one step from
there and see what happens!

19
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:56,760
I'll help this guy from here!

20
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,300
Help!

21
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:03,300
W-what should we do?

22
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:05,460
The way he's acting, he might really do it!

23
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:07,680
Anyway, we need to calm him down right now.

24
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:11,360
Argh! Why do we have to go about
it in such a roundabout way?!

25
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:13,600
Ryotsu!

26
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:14,320
One at a time!

27
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,700
This is obviously the quicker way.

28
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:32,380
Ryo-chan's going to sneak around
underneath and catch the culprit.

29
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,600
Right, we need to distract the perp.

30
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:38,360
Hey, what do you want? Tell us.

31
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,640
Get me 50 million yen in cash.

32
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:44,280
So, 50 million in cash, right?

33
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:47,180
Got it. Can I buy a 10,000-yen... or what?

34
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:52,620
And a car! Get me a car!

35
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:53,760
Got it!

36
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,360
Don't forget to fill it up with gas!

37
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:00,880
Any other demands, or not?

38
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:01,940
Anything else!

39
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:03,080
Anything else...

40
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:06,140
Not so fast!

41
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:09,840
We did it!

42
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,420
It's all right now!

43
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,400
Hey, give up already!

44
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,300
You bastard!

45
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:25,740
How about that?

46
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:27,780
Senpai

47
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:29,280
Good job, Ryotsu!

48
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:32,500
Oh no, Ryotsu, run!

49
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:37,640
Dad

50
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,100
Aaaaaah!

51
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:50,660
Ryotsu!

52
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:51,740
Senpai!

53
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,180
Ryo-chan!

54
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:57,100
Ryo-chan!

55
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:02,460
Ryo-chan! Ryo-chan!

56
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:04,540
Don't worry.

57
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:07,580
That guy would be fine
even if a tank ran over him.

58
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:08,500
But...

59
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:11,100
He's always been fine up until now.

60
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:13,180
I'm sure he'll be fine this time too.

61
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:13,900
Yeah.

62
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:18,660
That one was really rough, though.

63
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,860
Ryo-chan!

64
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:26,520
Hey, Reiko, don't worry.

65
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,560
I'm perfectly fine, as you can see!

66
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:30,480
He still hasn't come up.

67
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:32,000
Is he really all right?

68
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,120
I'm right here, see? Right here!

69
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:36,900
It was quite a shock, after all.

70
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:38,800
Hey, Nakagawa, what's with you too?

71
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:39,400
Senpai.

72
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,060
It's just like him.

73
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:44,120
He's probably hiding somewhere,
trying to scare us.

74
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:48,000
Ugh, are you all making fun of me?

75
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:50,280
He's not here.

76
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,400
I told you, I'm right here!

77
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:55,760
What's that?

78
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:59,220
Chief, this is serious, it's a disaster!

79
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:02,860
Senpai, he usually pops back up about now.

80
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:04,580
Anyway, let's look for the tiles.

81
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:06,060
Ugh, how frustrating!

82
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,520
A police officer!

83
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,680
Rolled-up sleeves, sandals on his feet...

84
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:16,200
Haven't I seen him somewhere?

85
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:18,200
It's me.

86
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:20,660
It's just me.

87
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:22,900
Somehow, I feel like I've seen him before.

88
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:24,600
Me.

89
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,480
I'm here, and...

90
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,100
this one's me too.

91
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,760
So then, what on earth...

92
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:31,840
I'm floating...

93
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:34,900
That means... did I actually die?

94
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:37,400
No way!

95
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:39,260
Hey, pull yourself together!

96
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:43,580
I haven't even beaten the new game yet!

97
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:45,360
Hey, hold on, you!

98
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:46,720
Excuse me, you!

99
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,720
Goo-gonichiwa...
(Hello, or rather a garbled greeting)

100
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:52,220
It's a ghost!

101
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:54,540
Whoa, a ghost! Stay away!

102
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:57,160
Judging by your appearance, I thought so.

103
00:05:58,080 --> 00:06:02,160
You're not officially dead yet, you know.

104
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,540
But I have legs, right?

105
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:07,580
You can still go back.

106
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:09,820
Really? What do I do?

107
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:17,180
It's easy. Just dive into your body
as if you're lying down on top of it.

108
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,180
Alright!

109
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:19,620
Mm.

110
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:27,540
I'm back to life! Of course,
you can come and go as you please.

111
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:31,940
Well, this is great! I'm alive again!

112
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:36,320
It's what they call an
out-of-body experience.

113
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:38,260
People can't see it, though,

114
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:41,880
but we real ghosts can see it.

115
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:43,860
So that's why Reiko and the others

116
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:45,540
couldn't see me?

117
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:47,720
I'm like an invisible man, then.

118
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:50,380
Is there anything else I can do?

119
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:51,480
Well, let me think.

120
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:53,860
Fly through the sky,

121
00:06:53,860 --> 00:06:57,120
and you can slip into other people, too.

122
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:57,700
What?

123
00:06:57,700 --> 00:07:01,320
Mostly, anything unconscious,
you can get into.

124
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:03,940
Still, I envy you.

125
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:07,840
I don't have a body to return to anymore,
you see.

126
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:10,880
I've been a ghost for eight years.

127
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,540
If you can return to your
own body whenever you like,

128
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:17,060
there's no reason not to make use of this.

129
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:17,920
Senpai!

130
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:19,980
Yo-chan.

131
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:21,360
Senpai!

132
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:23,660
Stop hiding and show yourself!

133
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:26,160
Well, I'll be off, then.

134
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,860
Thanks for everything.

135
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:31,660
Yeah, if I really die, let's meet again!

136
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:33,040
Senpai!

137
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:38,520
That's Senpai's... Chief! He's here!

138
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:40,360
Ryo-chan!

139
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:41,380
Ryotsu!

140
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:49,880
Ryo-chan!

141
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:53,140
Reiko!

142
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:54,420
Ryotsu!

143
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:58,100
Hey, Ryotsu! Open your eyes! Ryotsu!

144
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,680
Oh no, I've gotta get back in there first.

145
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:04,300
Wait, let me try it out right away.

146
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,520
Reiko-san, Reiko-san.

147
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:07,700
Heh, there we go.

148
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:12,220
Reiko-san.

149
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:12,700
What?

150
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,160
Reiko-san.

151
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:18,700
Oh no, I just suddenly
remembered I have something to do.

152
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:19,680
Excuse me.

153
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:21,020
Reiko-san.

154
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:24,400
I'm Reiko.

155
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,940
Hahahahaha.

156
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:36,320
Yes, yes, sorry about that, okay?

157
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:38,940
Sis, you've got a really nice pair,
haven't you?

158
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:45,560
This is heaven, man.

159
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,380
Oh

160
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:53,660
Wahahahaha!

161
00:08:53,660 --> 00:08:56,400
I soaked too long and got dizzy.

162
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,920
Now, what's next...

163
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:05,000
Lemons?
Ryo-chan's always causing me trouble, so...

164
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:10,020
Just a little present.
Being rich really is nice, isn't it?

165
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:19,740
Somehow Ryo-san has gotten coarse... I
wonder if it's the effect of mass production.

166
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:25,240
What should I do next...
And now, the violent criminal.

167
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:29,200
Kyūchi Yoshiyuki was struck by a train while being arrested,
fell into the river, and died in the line of duty.

168
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:31,880
Here is a follow-up on Senior
Patrol Officer Kankichi Ryotsu.

169
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:34,180
That's me!

170
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:37,860
At Katsushika Police Station, in recognition
of Senior Patrol Officer Ryotsu's achievements,

171
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:41,340
we have decided to award a two-rank
posthumous promotion and a special bonus.

172
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:43,620
A bonus? Now that's more like it!

173
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:47,040
We now take you live from
Katsushika Police Station.

174
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:53,200
Where's the camera?

175
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,520
For our senior officer to die like this...

176
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:33,400
Life is full of surprises.
You never know what's coming next.

177
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:37,280
Poor Maria-chan was so
shocked she took to her bed.

178
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:42,060
Now, let us express our condolences to Officer Ryotsu,
who died in the line of duty.

179
00:10:42,060 --> 00:10:44,280
I'd like us to observe a moment of silence.

180
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:45,620
Everyone, a moment of silence.

181
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:57,660
First, we'll have to knock him out.

182
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:04,420
Yeah! Is everybody with me?

183
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:07,880
The earlier announcement was a mistake.

184
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:10,720
Officer Kankichi Ryotsu's bonus is 15 yen.

185
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:12,760
His rank is promoted
two levels posthumously.

186
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:17,780
Also, starting today, everyone's
uniforms will follow Dekapan's example.

187
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:20,120
The men will wear nothing
but their underpants.

188
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:24,980
That means Dekapan
Officer and Brief Jun-san.

189
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:27,720
What is this?

190
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:30,200
What do you think you're doing?

191
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,860
Everyone, take your clothes off, quickly!

192
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:33,380
It's the chief's orders!

193
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:34,820
No way...

194
00:11:35,540 --> 00:11:36,780
What's going on?

195
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:39,500
But if it's the chief's orders...

196
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,220
If it's come to this...

197
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:49,140
What was I doing?

198
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:54,420
Hey, you came to, Reiko?

199
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:01,120
Ugh.

200
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:06,400
I'm skinny, so I'm not confident
doing this kind of thing.

201
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:09,500
Even if you were confident,
this is definitely perverted.

202
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:14,360
Very well, then from now on,
instead of a salute, the greeting is this.

203
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:17,340
Ohohoi poyo!

204
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:19,360
Ew! Pervert!

205
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:24,180
Hey! How dare you call the chief a pervert!

206
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:26,760
Because a pervert is a pervert!

207
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:27,920
That's right, that's right!

208
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:33,140
I almost forgot! The subordinates'
uniforms should also follow Dekapan's style!

209
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:39,240
If you don't follow orders,
I'll fire every one of you!

210
00:12:49,340 --> 00:12:50,300
Naoka!

211
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:56,900
Naoka, Naoka, pull yourself together!

212
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:00,760
Ugly!

213
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:02,680
What did you just say?

214
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:05,560
Well, it's the truth!

215
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:09,060
Ugly, ugly!
Ugly face, and an even uglier personality!

216
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:09,775
What's that supposed to mean?

217
00:13:09,825 --> 00:13:13,600
You're as flat as a board yourself,
hiding it with padding!

218
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:15,992
Hmph, I know everything. Deep down, you

219
00:13:16,042 --> 00:13:18,100
had a crush on Kankichi Ryotsu, didn't you?

220
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:20,060
Hey, who are you calling a caveman!

221
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:21,080
A caveman?!

222
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:25,920
You're a caveman, so I called you a caveman!
A vulgar, filthy, short-legged caveman with a gorilla face!

223
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:32,940
Yes, got you!

224
00:13:32,940 --> 00:13:34,860
Don't you "hmm" me!

225
00:13:34,860 --> 00:13:37,380
Flat-chested Buriko,
you're the one who's ugly on the inside!

226
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:38,600
What did you say?

227
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,760
Just the other day,
in the laundry room at the bathhouse,

228
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:42,100
you were puffing out your
chest and holding a sanka.

229
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:43,400
Serves you right!

230
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:44,540
That's payback for all
the grudges I've held!

231
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:45,840
No!

232
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:48,120
I left my model kit in
front of the electronics shop!

233
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:50,980
Chief, Chief!

234
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:53,960
You've come to!

235
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,540
What on earth happened to me?

236
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:58,760
Come on, everyone!
A new greeting for the Chief!

237
00:13:58,760 --> 00:13:59,520
Sir!

238
00:14:00,490 --> 00:14:01,900
Hoooy!

239
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:03,980
Whoa!

240
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,660
Hoooy!

241
00:14:05,660 --> 00:14:06,540
Whoa!

242
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,620
Bakabon!

243
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:25,520
Bakabon!

244
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:29,340
That concludes our report. Furthermore,
the body of the fallen Officer Ryotsu

245
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:32,700
will be cremated at a later
date due to funeral arrangements.

246
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:39,700
Hey, what's the big rush this evening?
I'd better get back into my body quickly.

247
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:43,340
Aaaah! I'm trying to say it, so why...?

248
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:43,920
I'm gonna crash into it!

249
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:45,200
Me

250
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:50,580
Chief

251
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:52,960
Idiot!

252
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:57,480
That's dangerous, Chief!

253
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:59,140
I'm not the Chief.

254
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:00,760
I am the Grim Reaper.

255
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:01,780
Grim Reaper

256
00:15:01,780 --> 00:15:02,360
That's right.

257
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:04,240
I've come to fetch you.

258
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:06,220
Come quietly and follow me.

259
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:09,420
Wait a moment, please.

260
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:11,440
I have no business with some Grim Reaper.

261
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:13,720
Even if you don't have it there,
I have it here.

262
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:17,820
You're already dead, you know.

263
00:15:17,820 --> 00:15:19,480
That's got to be some kind of mistake.

264
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:22,540
The ghost from earlier
said I'm not dead yet...

265
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:26,820
Heh, time's up.

266
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:28,640
No way, I refuse.

267
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:31,480
Fine, you really don't know when to give up.

268
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:36,640
Kankichi Ryotsu, Katsushika Ward, Tokyo.
Exclusively of the Tsukudani shop,

269
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:38,820
was born as the eldest
son of a general store.

270
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:43,900
Father: Ginji. Mother: Yone.
June 14, Heisei 10.

271
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:47,560
Suddenly struck by a train,
he fell into a river and died.

272
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:49,520
There's no mistake.

273
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:52,940
No mistake? That can't be right!

274
00:15:52,940 --> 00:15:55,340
I have no intention of going to heaven yet.

275
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:57,720
Idiot! Who said anything about heaven?

276
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:00,780
You were destined for hell on your third day of life,
you know.

277
00:16:00,780 --> 00:16:01,740
Don't joke around!

278
00:16:01,740 --> 00:16:02,720
Then bring me back to life!

279
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:04,080
Just come with me.

280
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:06,680
No.

281
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:11,000
I'm not going to just die quietly.

282
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:18,080
I'll rewrite this guy's data.

283
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,340
Hey, Ryotsu!

284
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:23,260
Wait, Ryotsu!

285
00:16:24,380 --> 00:16:25,240
As if I'd wait!

286
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:26,600
Stop!

287
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:31,940
It's a dead end.

288
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:35,420
At this rate, I can't even possess someone.

289
00:16:35,420 --> 00:16:36,440
Ryotsu.

290
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:47,180
Phew.

291
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:49,980
Ah!

292
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:53,160
Come on, Ryo-zu! Which one did you possess?

293
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:56,600
You?! You?! You?!

294
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:58,220
Ugh...

295
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:04,320
Naive, naive. You think I'd possess
something as ordinary as that?

296
00:17:07,820 --> 00:17:12,100
Let's see, the future prime minister,
with an annual income of 30 billion yen.

297
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:14,700
And a lifespan of about 1,200 years.

298
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:20,060
Damn it, no matter how much your lifespan grows,
there's nothing you can do if your body gets scrapped.

299
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:31,580
I'm not used to flying yet,
so this is really exhausting.

300
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:33,420
But I think I made it in time somehow.

301
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:37,160
Namu namu gachan gachan

302
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:40,380
Gachan gachan namu namu

303
00:17:40,380 --> 00:17:43,640
Namu namu gachan gachan

304
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:47,520
Namu namu gachan gachan

305
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:50,400
That Ryo-san would end up like this...

306
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:51,900
I can't believe it, can we?

307
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:55,540
Ryo-san, why, why?

308
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:57,520
Are you really that sad that I died?

309
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:58,860
You're making me cry.

310
00:17:58,860 --> 00:18:02,720
Why didn't you pay back
your debts before you died?

311
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:06,560
Damn it.

312
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:12,180
There's quite a lot of condolence money here

313
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:14,680
This should rightfully go
to the dead man himself.

314
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:16,620
So that means it's my money.

315
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:18,380
What an idiot.

316
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:21,480
Honestly, what an idiot.

317
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:23,440
This is ridiculous.

318
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:26,820
Even after I've become a Buddha,
I still get scolded?

319
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:29,260
Ugh, this is so annoying.

320
00:18:29,260 --> 00:18:30,580
Why did you have to die?

321
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:31,620
Condolence telegram.

322
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:32,960
Chief.

323
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:34,740
Do you really dislike me that much?

324
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:42,840
Take this!

325
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:46,040
Gachon-gen-gen, Kōden thief!

326
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,160
Looks like we've caught the Kōden thief!

327
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:57,300
Come quietly with me.

328
00:18:57,820 --> 00:19:00,560
Why does the Grim Reaper have a stun gun?

329
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:04,440
The other world is also linked
to progress in the real world.

330
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:05,780
Come on, then.

331
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:06,580
Look at this.

332
00:19:06,580 --> 00:19:09,200
I've been set to live
until I'm 1,200 years old.

333
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,780
I've got no business with you.

334
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:12,280
You idiot.

335
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:14,200
Because I entered some absurd data.

336
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:16,960
An error came up on the Grim
Reaper headquarters' computer.

337
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,360
That's invalid.

338
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:18,700
What?

339
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:21,300
As fate decrees, today you

340
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:22,860
Let's go!

341
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:25,660
No, it's no good!

342
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:27,020
The thief is getting away!

343
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:27,960
I know that already!

344
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:29,960
I won't let him get away!

345
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:32,100
That's my money!

346
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:33,480
Hey, Ryo-zu!

347
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:34,140
Stop!

348
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,060
Stop that bus!

349
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:47,960
Damn it, I'll fly after it, yah!

350
00:19:48,220 --> 00:19:50,240
Running would've been faster, wouldn't it!

351
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:53,120
Yes, sir!

352
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:56,940
Now we will carry out the coffin.

353
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:11,100
Commencing my Gyoden!

354
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:16,000
Damn it!
Does it have to be a living, physical body?

355
00:20:19,780 --> 00:20:21,180
I have no choice at this point!

356
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:22,020
Fire!

357
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:25,620
Woah-aaah!

358
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,100
Wait!

359
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:30,460
Turn around!

360
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:32,040
My coordination!

361
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:36,780
Stop!

362
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:38,620
Why is an old lady here!

363
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:44,220
Damn it, quick,
the old lady's going into cardiac arrest!

364
00:20:44,540 --> 00:20:46,940
At this rate,
this old lady will stop breathing!

365
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:50,820
Ugh

366
00:20:51,660 --> 00:20:53,260
Hyah!

367
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:54,260
Whoa!

368
00:20:54,780 --> 00:20:55,320
There!

369
00:20:57,520 --> 00:21:00,620
Wah wah wah wah wah! Wait, I'm telling you!

370
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:05,660
W-what on earth is going on here!

371
00:21:10,660 --> 00:21:12,100
At this rate, he'll get away!

372
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:12,680
Hah!

373
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:13,580
It's now or never!

374
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:17,960
Yes!

375
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,200
Get back here!

376
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:23,040
Give back my discharge!

377
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:25,520
Why is there a bucket?!

378
00:21:26,220 --> 00:21:26,860
Whoa!

379
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:27,800
Whoa!

380
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:30,080
Whoa!

381
00:21:30,180 --> 00:21:30,800
Whoa!

382
00:21:32,780 --> 00:21:34,360
You've caused us so much trouble.

383
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:40,720
Oh no, this won't do!

384
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:42,380
That was my hearse!

385
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:45,000
My money!

386
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:46,340
Whoa!

387
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:48,800
Damn you, you...

388
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:50,240
Damn it, I can't grab it!

389
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:51,120
Whoa!

390
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:56,180
This isn't the time for this!

391
00:21:58,860 --> 00:21:59,660
That's it.

392
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:02,420
Don't joke with me!
I was ready to die giving up that money!

393
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:04,800
I'm already dead, anyway! Let's go!

394
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:07,580
I'm not going to hell!

395
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:22,400
This is it, goodbye, Ryotsu.

396
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:25,460
your model kits and game
software you collected,

397
00:22:25,460 --> 00:22:27,420
we'll put them in the coffin with you.

398
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:29,280
And your filthy videos too.

399
00:22:34,540 --> 00:22:36,400
Now, we will close the lid.

400
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:40,600
Duplicates, duplicates.
Don't hesitate, just rest in peace.

401
00:22:49,540 --> 00:22:52,040
Damn it, where is my body?

402
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:55,320
Gah, take this!

403
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:00,760
Too bad, Ryotsu.

404
00:23:00,760 --> 00:23:02,440
What?!

405
00:23:03,020 --> 00:23:05,200
I'm not dying yet!

406
00:23:09,820 --> 00:23:11,240
Now, we will carry him out.

407
00:23:17,460 --> 00:23:19,220
M-my body's...

408
00:23:19,220 --> 00:23:21,980
Damn it, give up already!

409
00:23:22,740 --> 00:23:24,280
I can still make it!

410
00:23:29,860 --> 00:23:31,860
Yes! I did it!

411
00:23:31,860 --> 00:23:34,440
Adieu!

412
00:23:35,820 --> 00:23:36,160
What?

413
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:39,840
Adieu!

414
00:23:39,980 --> 00:23:40,800
Oof! Heave-ho!

415
00:23:40,980 --> 00:23:41,560
Shunpon!

416
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:43,660
Somebody put out the fire, put out the fire!

417
00:23:43,900 --> 00:23:45,140
Whyyyyyy?!

418
00:23:47,120 --> 00:23:50,040
Having a guy like him come
to hell would be a nuisance.

419
00:23:50,180 --> 00:23:52,460
I'm never coming to fetch him again.

420
00:23:52,740 --> 00:23:54,980
Somebody! Put out the fire!

421
00:23:55,620 --> 00:23:57,140
I'm going to die again!

422
00:24:03,620 --> 00:24:04,020
Chief,

423
00:24:04,070 --> 00:24:07,820
Why on earth are we
stuck together like this?

424
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:09,800
Get off me, Chief.

425
00:24:09,800 --> 00:24:11,520
Where are you going?

426
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:14,280
I don't want to go to a place like that.

427
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:16,900
Stop it, Chief.

428
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:20,000
Next time: Dangerous Duo in Close Contact

429
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,040
Chief.

430
00:24:35,700 --> 00:24:44,040
With surprise, with commotion, with spirit,
with resolve, with quick hands, with a helping hand

431
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:55,700
decided with flashes of inspiration, bouncing along,
wrapping it up, taking action, soaring away

432
00:24:56,600 --> 00:25:00,040
Above all, an incredible power

433
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:06,420
Gather everyone, come here

434
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:12,680
A dreamlike, final energy

435
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:17,120
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday

436
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:20,020
Painting the universe,
standing on the ground

437
00:25:20,020 --> 00:25:23,820
Kameari's star spins around,
drawing a circle

438
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:27,480
This should be fine, right?

439
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:28,960
Like hell it is!

440
00:25:42,520 --> 00:25:43,920
Thank you for watching.

